[{:db/id 17592186152204 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152206 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" "question-04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" :question/id #uuid "ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" :question/math-academy-id "q-86866" :question/problem "![](images/51/51706be38cc1c72079fe702c899b575ea53ba4d85e7990a6aa81f20dc8da4de3.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$\n- ${∬}_{R}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-5,5]\\times [0,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e76b06d-2177-5f41-ae22-04ed4efb0ed9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e76b06d-2177-5f41-ae22-04ed4efb0ed9" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e76b06d-2177-5f41-ae22-04ed4efb0ed9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-784f60d8-744f-5a20-8590-4309ac0a7fb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7ac4f900-28cf-5d47-aca1-6ede50a776f2" "answer-784f60d8-744f-5a20-8590-4309ac0a7fb3" "answer-c63263fe-1e9f-59ea-a5b6-858826246c29" "answer-fdc6305c-bf3a-5c13-af4f-f56b112873c5" "answer-657bd7d3-dd1c-5d1e-a2e2-e5779123f72b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ac4f900-28cf-5d47-aca1-6ede50a776f2" :answer/id #uuid "7ac4f900-28cf-5d47-aca1-6ede50a776f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-784f60d8-744f-5a20-8590-4309ac0a7fb3" :answer/id #uuid "784f60d8-744f-5a20-8590-4309ac0a7fb3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c63263fe-1e9f-59ea-a5b6-858826246c29" :answer/id #uuid "c63263fe-1e9f-59ea-a5b6-858826246c29" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdc6305c-bf3a-5c13-af4f-f56b112873c5" :answer/id #uuid "fdc6305c-bf3a-5c13-af4f-f56b112873c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-657bd7d3-dd1c-5d1e-a2e2-e5779123f72b" :answer/id #uuid "657bd7d3-dd1c-5d1e-a2e2-e5779123f72b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68" :question/id #uuid "04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68" :question/math-academy-id "q-129786" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9d66cb97b9e04367ce2250e5156eaa9daaf42fadb395220e0464bca687e91908.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,4]$\n- ${∬}_{R}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-4,4]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-785531fb-5cc7-5887-a5ee-25914bfbfc99"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-785531fb-5cc7-5887-a5ee-25914bfbfc99" :answer-field/id #uuid "785531fb-5cc7-5887-a5ee-25914bfbfc99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-69f11751-9b65-5442-9be4-dfc89e4dd373" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69f11751-9b65-5442-9be4-dfc89e4dd373" "answer-f33c6146-83ba-5ed5-bb69-2dc2054153f6" "answer-197936d1-4a7e-51b8-91f0-94b31cb7063c" "answer-8ce4e9eb-5239-59bf-9aa9-acfacda1c294" "answer-4012db07-82ce-5c39-93dc-c15349b6c4fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69f11751-9b65-5442-9be4-dfc89e4dd373" :answer/id #uuid "69f11751-9b65-5442-9be4-dfc89e4dd373" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f33c6146-83ba-5ed5-bb69-2dc2054153f6" :answer/id #uuid "f33c6146-83ba-5ed5-bb69-2dc2054153f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-197936d1-4a7e-51b8-91f0-94b31cb7063c" :answer/id #uuid "197936d1-4a7e-51b8-91f0-94b31cb7063c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ce4e9eb-5239-59bf-9aa9-acfacda1c294" :answer/id #uuid "8ce4e9eb-5239-59bf-9aa9-acfacda1c294" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4012db07-82ce-5c39-93dc-c15349b6c4fe" :answer/id #uuid "4012db07-82ce-5c39-93dc-c15349b6c4fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34" :question/id #uuid "bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34" :question/math-academy-id "q-129908" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-1$ and $y=2-|x|.$ If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/1a/1a5369b58b14444c5ea0ce4bb36954d1d0b7964dcef4e95f9cc527694b3a9e4f.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- Functions I and III equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and equal $0$ outside $D.$\n\n- We cannot use function II. The function is not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(1,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the function is nonzero at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-97a4c622-55f3-52fb-965d-fe7f4db5d8a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97a4c622-55f3-52fb-965d-fe7f4db5d8a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "97a4c622-55f3-52fb-965d-fe7f4db5d8a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0575dc8f-eac3-5b1e-a66b-25c751aa05e9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c78122a-3a25-5733-8658-cd93b68aea0e" "answer-0575dc8f-eac3-5b1e-a66b-25c751aa05e9" "answer-3c793446-7160-555d-ab53-99c4b0187b99" "answer-57aebbe5-21ba-5866-a272-d33fb018e22f" "answer-4b681d8b-d313-54f5-a6b1-5e551fd84bef"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c78122a-3a25-5733-8658-cd93b68aea0e" :answer/id #uuid "1c78122a-3a25-5733-8658-cd93b68aea0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0575dc8f-eac3-5b1e-a66b-25c751aa05e9" :answer/id #uuid "0575dc8f-eac3-5b1e-a66b-25c751aa05e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c793446-7160-555d-ab53-99c4b0187b99" :answer/id #uuid "3c793446-7160-555d-ab53-99c4b0187b99" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57aebbe5-21ba-5866-a272-d33fb018e22f" :answer/id #uuid "57aebbe5-21ba-5866-a272-d33fb018e22f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b681d8b-d313-54f5-a6b1-5e551fd84bef" :answer/id #uuid "4b681d8b-d313-54f5-a6b1-5e551fd84bef" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b8cf7360-113f-5967-a53f-923c8be1dfcf" :activity/id #uuid "b8cf7360-113f-5967-a53f-923c8be1dfcf" :activity/title "Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049235 :activity/course 17592186046665 :activity/steps ["step-4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" "step-080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" "step-5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" "step-30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" "step-98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb"] :activity/first-step "step-4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" :step/id #uuid "4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" :step/content 17592186152832 :step/next "step-080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" :step/id #uuid "080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" :step/content 17592186152833 :step/next "step-5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" :step/id #uuid "5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" :step/content "question-ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" :step/next "step-30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" :step/id #uuid "30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" :step/content "question-04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68" :step/next "step-98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb" :step/id #uuid "98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb" :step/content "question-bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
